  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many servings of peanut butter Toby should add to his toast to reach a total of 500 calories, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the calories from the bread: Toby has one piece of bread, which has 100 calories.\n2. Determine the remaining calories needed: Since Toby wants a total of 500 calories, we subtract the calories from the bread from the total desired calories.\n   \\[\n   500 - 100 = 400\n   \\]\n   So, Toby needs 400 more calories from the peanut butter.\n3. Calculate the number of servings of peanut butter needed: Each serving of peanut butter has 200 calories. To find out how many servings are needed to get 400 calories, we divide 400 by 200.\n   \\[\n   \\frac{400}{200} = 2\n   \\]\n   Therefore, Toby should add 2 servings of peanut butter.\n\nThe final answer is \\boxed{2}.",
